  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes QFedFisher, a variational quantum federated learning method that uses layer-wise Fisher information to preserve important client parameters during aggregation. On ADNI, it reports 89.9% testing accuracy with 0.278 loss over 100 communication rounds on 10 clients; on MNIST, it reports 91.2% accuracy with 0.418 loss over 300 rounds on 100 clients, outperforming QFedAvg and QFedAdam in both cases.",
